#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d59ac953-c511-5d6f-902d-4aeb804c99ce" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of the Hermitian Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aab14461-fafd-5ce8-a827-b7fbcd8ba123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4+8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333366} {:answer/id #uuid "632d4c5b-412e-5d54-8287-deafd0eb4f50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333367} {:answer/id #uuid "bbb1f13b-8ee6-5ffa-a10a-2c6c4e3eeb9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11+8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333368} {:answer/id #uuid "5673cb0f-58ae-5230-9bed-341314357b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4+11\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333369} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a10379-ceca-5e6e-8aa5-185c292e236c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7+6\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5673cb0f-58ae-5230-9bed-341314357b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4+11\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333369} :answer-field/id #uuid "bccea3f0-485f-5dae-94e4-fcbdad249dfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0f409f0a-d1f3-5a6f-b4c4-c490f83517f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141162" :question/problem "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,2b+(3-2\\text{i})c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=1-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,c⟩=3\\text{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,2b+(3-2\\text{i})c⟩ & =⟨a,2b⟩+⟨a,(3-2\\text{i})c⟩ \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{2}⟨a,b⟩+(\\overset{―}{3-2\\text{i}})⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨a,b⟩+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,b⟩+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩ & =2\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨a,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩ & =2\\cdot \\overset{―}{1-\\text{i}}+(3+2\\text{i})\\cdot (3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (1+\\text{i})-6+9\\text{i} \\\\  & =-4+11\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d59ac953-c511-5d6f-902d-4aeb804c99ce" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of the Hermitian Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "708e87bf-0009-52aa-a36d-60eb806f7f03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333373} {:answer/id #uuid "4bc6aff1-cee8-5a14-848d-6ce0a2bf9575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333374} {:answer/id #uuid "18a3c178-1ff7-5dbe-8f43-909f93b3cd04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333375} {:answer/id #uuid "05ac0162-68fd-579d-a436-b9959555b924" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+5\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333376} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3075fc-47fc-505e-a92d-6e8cd526f02c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05ac0162-68fd-579d-a436-b9959555b924" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+5\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333376} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0ec2b6a-0e60-5928-bcbc-9af9c861bb3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd73aa00-9e5a-5eba-8caf-b97d3032b2dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-97200" :question/problem "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨\\text{i}a,\\,b+c⟩$ if \n\n  $⟨a,b⟩=3-2\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨c,a⟩=2+\\text{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\text{i}a,\\,b+c⟩ & =⟨\\text{i}a,b⟩+⟨\\text{i}a,c⟩ \\\\  & =\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}⟨a,c⟩ & =\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨a,b⟩$ and $⟨c,a⟩:$    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩} & =\\text{i}(3-2\\text{i})+\\text{i}\\overset{―}{(2+\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\text{i}(3-2\\text{i})+\\text{i}(2-\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2+3\\text{i}+1+2\\text{i} \\\\  & =3+5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
